    "terminal_reason": "completed",
    "result_text": "I implemented `build_client` in `app/llm_client.py` and added tests for it. All 3 tests pass, including the existing one.\n\nOne thing that shaped the code: the pinned `openai==3.19.2` uses **`httpx2`**, not `httpx`. So the HTTP client is an `httpx2.Client`, and `httpx` would fail to import. `httpx2` is already installed as an openai dependency, so nothing new was added.\n\n**What `build_client` does:**\n- **Timeouts:** connect 5s; read, write and pool 30s. These are set on both the HTTP client and the `OpenAI` client. That's needed because the SDK sends its own timeout with every request, which overrides whatever the HTTP client has.\n- **Retries:** `max_retries=2`.\n- **Logging:** a `\"request\"` event hook logs `\"<METHOD> <URL>\"` at INFO on the `app.http` logger. The hook runs every time a request is sent, so retries and redirects are logged too.\n- **Transport:** passed straight to the HTTP client. With `None`, the normal network transport is used.\n- **HTTP client:** built with openai's `DefaultHttpxClient`, so the SDK's usual connection limits and redirect handling still apply. A plain `httpx2.Client` would drop those.\n\n**Tests (`tests/test_llm_client.py`):**\n- They check the timeout values on both clients and that `max_retries` is 2.\n- With a stub transport that always returns HTTP 500, one `models.list()` call sends 3 requests through the stub (the first try plus 2 retries). It also logs exactly three `GET https://api.openai.com/v1/models` lines at INFO on `app.http`."
  },
